`P` does not have to be the printed normal form. The checker compares `P(b)` with the goal up to computation, so you can write the motive with your own source terms. Your reproducer checks with a one-line motive:

```bend
def composed(a):
  %eq_refl(unit(a, "x")) : {True{} == go(7n, Hold{_, String.append(unit(a, "x"), ","), unit(a, "x")}) : Bool}
  {==}
```

(with `law eq_refl: for s: String {True{} == String.eq(s, s) : Bool}`). On 2.0.31 the file prints `All terms check`; the only note is for the `@unsafe` stub of `eq_refl` that I used. Write the motive as the program writes the term, not as the printer shows it. So no new rewrite syntax is needed.

